  "description": "CR 207.2c, 701.9b, 107.3k, 601.2c, 602.5d, 122.1h, 715.3a, 702.10b: Rydia, Summoner of Mist's landfall trigger may discard a card to draw one; its {X}, {T} ability returns target Saga card with mana value X from its controller's graveyard with a finality counter, and the Saga gains haste until end of turn",
  "note": "Two cards in hand make the discard a choice. With X = 3, the Centaur Courser (mana value 3, no Saga) and Summon: Valefor (a Saga, mana value 5) are no legal targets; History of Benalia (a Saga, mana value 3) is a second legal one, so the target is asked. Summon: Choco/Mog (a Saga creature, mana value 3) comes back with its lore counter and a finality counter, and attacks the turn it returns. The rummage's land is played after the activation, so no untapped land asks for an extra mana source. On turn 3 alice declines the landfall rummage and keeps her hand. With the chapter II trigger on the stack on turn 3, the Summon ability can't be activated (sorcery timing).",
